{"name":"Orange Peel","hex":"#ffa000","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"orange peel","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The skin of an orange, including the pith.","An uneven surface resembling orange peel, especially cellulite or an imperfect finish on a spray-painted object such as a car."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/orange_peel"}],"entries":[{"title":"Orange peel (effect)","blocks":[{"text":"Orange peel is a certain kind of finish that may develop on painted and cast surfaces. The texture resembles the surface of the skin of an orange, hence the name \"orange peel\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Orange_Peel_Effect.jpg/330px-Orange_Peel_Effect.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orange_peel_(effect)"},{"title":"Orange Peel (horse)","blocks":[{"text":"Orange Peel was a Thoroughbred stallion that had a significant influence on the breeding of sport horses."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/DEAUVILLE%2C_4_Ao%C3%BBt._%E2%80%94L%27arriv%C3%A9e_du_PRIX_MAURICE_DE_GHEEST_%3B_GRILLEMONT_bat_ais%C3%A9ment_ORANGE_PEEL_et_SOLANGE.jpg/330px-DEAUVILLE%2C_4_Ao%C3%BBt._%E2%80%94L%27arriv%C3%A9e_du_PRIX_MAURICE_DE_GHEEST_%3B_GRILLEMONT_bat_ais%C3%A9ment_ORANGE_PEEL_et_SOLANGE.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orange_Peel_(horse)"},{"title":"Orange (fruit)","blocks":[{"text":"The orange, also called sweet orange to distinguish it from the bitter orange, is the fruit of a tree in the family Rutaceae. Botanically, this is the hybrid Citrus × sinensis, between the pomelo and the mandarin orange. The chloroplast genome, and therefore the maternal line, is that of pomelo. Hybrids of the sweet orange form later types of mandarin and the grapefruit. The sweet orange has had its full genome sequenced."}],"image":"